{"game": "roboquest", "language": "english", "appid": 692890, "month": "2026-09", "window": 4, "start_date": 1790121600, "end_date": 1790812799, "month_true_total": 90, "quota": 5, "returned": 5, "pulled_at": "2026-10-03 01:57:23 UTC", "reviews": [{"recommendationid": "236513632", "author": {"steamid": "76561198056562623", "personaname": "Liam", "persona_status": "offline", "profile_url": "https://steamcommunity.com/profiles/76561198056562623/", "num_games_owned": 0, "num_reviews": 2, "playtime_forever": 1311, "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0, "playtime_at_review": 1311, "last_played": 1733265311, "avatar": "be6f4690ab3012beb8cdd6230a3db004c3f3001a"}, "language": "english", "review": "A satisfying and engaging co-op experience that let a friend and I catch up weekly as we slowly worked through the campaign. Difficult enough to be keep your attention in moment to moment gameplay, but with enough breathing space that you can actually talk with the other player. We have played a few of these co-op rouge-likes and this is definitely one of the stronger ones.\r\n\r\nIts a frantic game where you will often be backed into a corner, but one where you can recognise how your own misplays bring about your failed runs. There is a definite run-to-run progression where your character gets stronger and your options increase as you play, but you also feel the gradual improvement in your own skill as you keep pushing through - meaning the game is more than just \"dying to get stronger\". \r\n\r\nReally appreciated the work done by the team on this game and looking forwards to seeing what the developers do next.", "timestamp_created": 1790730357, "timestamp_updated": 1790730357, "voted_up": true, "votes_up": 0, "votes_funny": 0, "weighted_vote_score": 0.5, "comment_count": 0, "steam_purchase": true, "received_for_free": false, "refunded": false, "written_during_early_access": false, "primarily_steam_deck": false, "app_release_date": "1597939791", "reactions": []}, {"recommendationid": "2